FOLLOW: Changing `LOG_ONLY` to `DEGRADE` forces the orchestration layer to actively manage models experiencing transient underperformance (e.g., via altered routing) rather than silently dropping the signal. Changing the default fallback to `EXCLUDE` guarantees the system fails closed by forcefully removing untrusted components if an unhandled failure type occurs. `DynamicManager` will process these states natively via its reallocation logic.

